  "statement": "There are `n` buildings along a road at distinct integer positions. You must install exactly `k` routers, each on a different building. Choose the buildings so that the **smallest distance between any two chosen routers is as large as possible**. Print that largest possible smallest distance.\n\n**Input.** First line `n k`. Second line the `n` positions (not necessarily sorted).\n\n**Output.** One integer.\n\n**Example.**\n\nInput:\n```\n5 3\n1 2 8 4 9\n```\nOutput:\n```\n3\n```",
  "constraints": [
    "2 ≤ k ≤ n ≤ 1000 in this browser version (the idea scales to 10^5)",
    "0 ≤ position ≤ 10^9, all positions distinct"
  ],
  "timeLimitMs": 1000,
