  "hints": [
    "If the minimum distance must be at least `d`, how would you greedily check whether `k` routers fit?",
    "Sort the positions. Place the first router at the leftmost building, then repeatedly take the next building at least `d` away.",
    "Feasibility is monotone in `d` (a larger `d` is harder). Binary search the largest `d` for which the greedy places at least `k` routers."
  ],
  "editorial": "Sort the positions. For a candidate distance `d`, the greedy 'always place at the leftmost allowed building' maximises the number of routers placed (an exchange argument: any valid placement can be shifted left without breaking spacing). So `ok(d)` = greedy count `>= k`.\n\n`ok` is monotone: if distance `d` works, every smaller distance works. Search the last true value in `[1, max - min]`; `ok(1)` is always true since positions are distinct and `k ≤ n`. Complexity `O(n log n + n log(max - min))`.\n\nUse `mid = (lo + hi + 1) / 2` when you set `lo = mid`, otherwise the loop can stall.",
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(n log n)",
    "space": "O(1)"
  },
  "starter": {
    "python": "import sys\n\n# Maximise the minimum gap between k chosen positions.\ndata = sys.stdin.read().split()\n# your code here\n",
    "javascript": "// Maximise the minimum gap between k chosen positions.\n// readLine() returns the next line of input (or null).\n// your code here\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    // Maximise the minimum gap between k chosen positions.\n    // your code here\n}\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner in = new Scanner(System.in);\n        // Maximise the minimum gap between k chosen positions.\n        // your code here\n    }\n}\n"
  },
  "solutions": {
    "python": "import sys\n\ndef main():\n    d = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    n, k = int(d[0]), int(d[1])\n    a = sorted(map(int, d[2:2 + n]))\n\n    def ok(dist):\n        placed, last = 1, a[0]\n        for x in a[1:]:\n            if x - last >= dist:\n                placed += 1\n                last = x\n        return placed >= k\n\n    lo, hi = 1, a[-1] - a[0]       # ok(lo) is true, find the last true\n    while lo < hi:\n        mid = (lo + hi + 1) // 2\n        if ok(mid):\n            lo = mid\n        else:\n            hi = mid - 1\n    print(lo)\n\nmain()\n",
    "javascript": "const __L = [];\nlet __s;\nwhile ((__s = readLine()) !== null) __L.push(__s);\nconst T = __L.join(' ').split(/\\s+/).filter((x) => x.length).map(Number);\nconst n = T[0], k = T[1];\nconst a = T.slice(2, 2 + n).sort((x, y) => x - y);\nfunction ok(dist) {\n  let placed = 1, last = a[0];\n  for (let i = 1; i < n; i++) {\n    if (a[i] - last >= dist) { placed++; last = a[i]; }\n  }\n  return placed >= k;\n}\nlet lo = 1, hi = a[n - 1] - a[0];\nwhile (lo < hi) {\n  const mid = Math.floor((lo + hi + 1) / 2);\n  if (ok(mid)) lo = mid; else hi = mid - 1;\n}\nconsole.log(String(lo));\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static StreamTokenizer st;\n\n    static long nl() throws IOException {\n        st.nextToken();\n        return (long) st.nval;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        st = new StreamTokenizer(new BufferedInputStream(System.in));\n        int n = (int) nl(), k = (int) nl();\n        long[] a = new long[n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) a[i] = nl();\n        Arrays.sort(a);\n        long lo = 1, hi = a[n - 1] - a[0];\n        while (lo < hi) {\n            long mid = (lo + hi + 1) / 2;\n            int placed = 1;\n            long last = a[0];\n            for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {\n                if (a[i] - last >= mid) { placed++; last = a[i]; }\n            }\n            if (placed >= k) lo = mid; else hi = mid - 1;\n        }\n        System.out.println(lo);\n    }\n}\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    int n, k;\n    scanf(\"%d %d\", &n, &k);\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (auto &v : a) scanf(\"%lld\", &v);\n    sort(a.begin(), a.end());\n    long long lo = 1, hi = a[n - 1] - a[0];\n    while (lo < hi) {\n        long long mid = (lo + hi + 1) / 2;\n        int placed = 1;\n        long long last = a[0];\n        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++)\n            if (a[i] - last >= mid) { placed++; last = a[i]; }\n        if (placed >= k) lo = mid; else hi = mid - 1;\n    }\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", lo);\n}\n"
  }
